From: Neutron lab (team agent live2) 2026-11-05
Subject: [PATCH] kernelbase: Issue an overlapped TransactNamedPipe as STATUS_PENDING.

What was seen (lab, Ableton Live 12.4.16 trial installer, Inno Setup 6.4.0): the install log says "Exception while
communicating with helper: Internal error: Helper: Response message has wrong size", "Helper process exited with
failure code: 0x700E8", "Failed to set permissions on directory (31)" for C:\ProgramData\Ableton\Live 12 Trial,
every run. Any Inno Setup 6 installer that uses its 64-bit helper (permissions, 64-bit COM/typelib registration)
hits the same path.

Mechanism: Inno's 32-bit Setup talks to its 64-bit helper over a message-mode named pipe. It zeroes an OVERLAPPED,
calls TransactNamedPipe(overlapped) (ERROR_IO_PENDING) and, when it has no message pump to run, goes straight to
GetOverlappedResult(wait=TRUE) (Setup.Helper.pas InternalCall). Wine's TransactNamedPipe, unlike its ReadFile,
WriteFile, DeviceIoControl and ConnectNamedPipe, did not set OVERLAPPED.Internal to STATUS_PENDING, and ntdll leaves
the IOSB alone while the transaction waits for the answer. GetOverlappedResult saw Internal 0 (success), returned
TRUE with 0 bytes at once, Inno raised "wrong size" and closed the pipe; the helper's WriteFile of its answer then
failed with ERROR_NO_DATA (232): exit code MAKELONG(232, 7) = 0x700E8, as logged.

Windows behavior: OVERLAPPED.Internal is documented as set to STATUS_PENDING when the request is issued; kernel32's
pipe tests (dlls/kernel32/tests/pipe.c) show Windows' ReadFile/WriteFile setting Internal and leaving InternalHigh.
Inno's code works on Windows (known-good). The probe team/live2/probe/pipeprobe32.exe + pipeprobe64.exe replays
the protocol (optional; not needed to settle this).

Fix: set overlapped->Internal = STATUS_PENDING before NtFsControlFile(FSCTL_PIPE_TRANSCEIVE), Internal only.
Kill switch: NEUTRON_TRANSACT_PENDING=0 (process environment).

Not covered: the "Need to restart Windows? Yes" at the end of the same install (VC++ 2013's Burn 3.7 elevated
engine scheduling the delete of its own running image; same on Windows, no change).

Lab evidence (runtime 11.10-182n = 182j + win32u (uah-menu-measure) + this kernelbase.dll x86_64/i386):
  probe pipeprobe32 (4 transactions, 2 without a message wait):
    182j:                         2/4 transactions read 0 bytes, helper exit 0x700e8
    182n on:                      4/4 read 16 bytes, helper exit 0 (2 runs)
    182n NEUTRON_TRANSACT_PENDING=0: 2/4 read 0 bytes (2 runs)
  full silent install of the Ableton installer into fresh copies of the lab prefix (Inno log):
    182n on:                      t3, t4 (final build) and t1, t2 (first build, also set InternalHigh=0): "Helper
                                  process exited.", no error, permissions set
    182n NEUTRON_TRANSACT_PENDING=0: x1, x2, x3 3/3 "Response message has wrong size", helper 0x700E8, "Failed to set
                                  permissions on directory (31)"
    182n before this dll (i1) and 182/182j (the ableton agent's ab1, ab2): same failure

--- a/dlls/kernelbase/sync.c
+++ b/dlls/kernelbase/sync.c
@@ -1656,9 +1656,26 @@
 
     if (overlapped)
     {
+        static int preset = -1;
+
         event = overlapped->hEvent;
         iosb = (IO_STATUS_BLOCK *)overlapped;
         if (((ULONG_PTR)event & 1) == 0) cvalue = overlapped;
+
+        /* NEUTRON neutron-transact-pending: issue the request as STATUS_PENDING, as ReadFile and WriteFile
+         * do (kernel32's pipe tests show Windows setting Internal, not InternalHigh) and as Windows documents
+         * for OVERLAPPED.Internal. The transaction completes only when the other end answers; until then
+         * ntdll leaves the IOSB alone, so a caller that zeroed its OVERLAPPED and went straight to
+         * GetOverlappedResult(wait) got "done, 0 bytes" at once. Inno Setup's 64-bit helper call does that
+         * ("Helper: Response message has wrong size", directory permissions not set).
+         * Kill switch: NEUTRON_TRANSACT_PENDING=0. */
+        if (preset < 0)
+        {
+            WCHAR value[2];
+            preset = !(GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"NEUTRON_TRANSACT_PENDING", value, ARRAY_SIZE(value) ) == 1
+                       && value[0] == '0');
+        }
+        if (preset) overlapped->Internal = STATUS_PENDING;
     }
     else
     {
